{"candidates":[{"content":"Keep the grounded extension as the pure label function over `att`, but make attack edges typed: each edge materialized from a warrant carriage carries a warrant-type tag (undercut vs. rebut vs. validity-closure), and the edge set is pre-processed by a fixed total preorder on types before the fixpoint runs. Because the preorder is total and a pure function of the graph, the resulting label assignment remains a deterministic, polynomial fixpoint; the typing adds discrimination power (e.g., a validity-closure attack outranks a rebut) without altering the uniqueness guarantee of the Dung grounded extension.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"0e806619395ec8f4","quote":"pure function of the graph"},{"block":"0378275f89478d38","quote":"Carriage is a relation, not a field"},{"block":"09ffabcd92979168","quote":"Dung grounded extension; unique, skeptical, polynomial"}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"src-8ddb400f3c2d52a681266c7cebc3b1898bac6750"}],"typicality":0.8},{"content":"Attach to every materialized attack edge its warrant-chain provenance so that each accepted node carries a traceable committed root. The carriage relation is the authority for warrant materialization; extend it with a provenance ledger recording, per attack edge, the chain of warrants and closures that produced it. Acceptance labels stay a pure function of the graph, so the fixpoint is untouched; the ledger makes 'validity of every committed root' checkable in polynomial time at commit time, converting a global invariant into a local per-edge certificate.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"0378275f89478d38","quote":"Carriage is a relation, not a field"},{"block":"0e806619395ec8f4","quote":"pure function of the graph"}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"src-8ddb400f3c2d52a681266c7cebc3b1898bac6750"}],"typicality":0.65},{"content":"After the skeptical fixpoint leaves some nodes suspended, run an advisory post-pass that ranks suspended nodes by defense depth: the number of distinct accepted defenders reachable via two attack steps (accepted -> attacker -> suspended). This never relabels a node, so determinism, polynomial cost, and reinstatement semantics are untouched — but it gives the loop a principled order for conjecture refinement and makes the suspended set's structure visible instead of a silent remainder. The grounded extension itself was never the problem; this targets what to do with its output.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"09ffabcd92979168","quote":"Dung grounded extension; unique, skeptical, polynomial"},{"block":"0c302d11d621778b","quote":"already a pure deterministic fixpoint"}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"src-8ddb400f3c2d52a681266c7cebc3b1898bac6750"}],"typicality":0.45},{"content":"Generalize the existing closure rule — any attacker of `validity_node` attacks the warrant — into a systematic family: every structural node (validity, internal consistency, coherence) generates an attack edge to its carrier's warrant, and the closure is computed to a fixed point before the grounded extension runs. The closure is a pure function of the graph (deterministic) with bounded fan-out (polynomial), so the fixpoint guarantees survive; this strengthens completeness of the attack graph so that no structural flaw can slip through as a silent suspension.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"0974daebd1665965","quote":"any attacker of `validity_node` attacks the warrant"},{"block":"0e806619395ec8f4","quote":"pure function of the graph"}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"src-8ddb400f3c2d52a681266c7cebc3b1898bac6750"}],"typicality":0.5},{"content":"Since the variator emits k bounded edits per step and most of the attack graph is unchanged, cache the prior label assignment and recompute only the affected subgraph, emitting a certificate that the result is the least fixed point. Determinism is preserved because the certificate verifies uniqueness of the fixpoint regardless of iteration order; cost stays polynomial and amortizes better than full recomputation because the edit is bounded and relabeling is monotone. This targets the real cost center — the edges, not the fixpoint — keeping the extension cheap enough to run at every loop step.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"0efee9d35ff76f87","quote":"variator emits k bounded edits"},{"block":"0c302d11d621778b","quote":"already a pure deterministic fixpoint"}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"src-8ddb400f3c2d52a681266c7cebc3b1898bac6750"}],"typicality":0.6},{"content":"Anchor attack-edge construction in cases: maintain a library of committed runs whose warrant-to-attack materializations are canonical, and calibrate the edge-construction rules (the `build_att` union) per case family so that the same warrant types yield the same attack patterns as the anchors. The label function stays pure and the fixpoint math is unchanged; what is strengthened is the quality of the attack graph itself — which is where the real work lives — making committed-root validity consistent with historical precedent rather than a per-run accident.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"0378275f89478d38","quote":"Carriage is a relation, not a field"},{"block":"0c302d11d621778b","quote":"already a pure deterministic fixpoint"},{"block":"0e806619395ec8f4","quote":"pure function of the graph"}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"src-8ddb400f3c2d52a681266c7cebc3b1898bac6750"}],"typicality":0.55}],"scratch_proposal":{"cluster_suggestions":[],"links":[],"new_blocks":[{"body":{"content":"Speculative: if attack edges are typed (Candidate 1), could the grounded extension be refined by a type-indexed defense relation — an edge defends only against attacks of a specific type? The total preorder guarantees determinism, but reinstatement would then be type-indexed rather than global. Does the least fixed point still coincide with the classic grounded extension, or does type-indexed reinstatement produce a distinct skeptical semantics that preserves 'reinstatement as a derived property' only within each type stratum? Need a counterexample hunt: can type-indexed defense yield a deterministic-but-non-grounded fixpoint, and if so does that violate the uniqueness guarantee or only the classical characterization?","possible_next_move":"Build a small enumeration over 3-4 node graphs with two attack types; check whether any deterministic type-indexed fixpoint differs from the grounded extension while still satisfying reinstatement within strata.","unfinished":"Formalize type-indexed defense as a modified characteristic function and test whether its least fixed point equals the classic grounded extension on small adversarial graphs.","why_keep_this":"The typed-attack idea is the strongest expansion candidate; this question probes whether typing can be pushed into defense without breaking the Dung-theoretic identity."},"local_key":"NEW_001"}],"revisions":[],"unresolved_questions":[{"question":"Does type-indexed defense (each attack edge defends only against attacks of a matching type) preserve uniqueness of the least fixed point, or can two fixpoints coexist under a total type preorder?","related_refs":["NEW_001"]}]},"simulation_proposals":[]}